{"companyInfo": {"Updated": "7/28/26", "Footnote": "Market value as of July 13, 2026.", "Country/Territory": "U.S.", "Headquarters": "Irvine, Tex.", "Industry": "Construction and Farm Machinery", "CEO": "Joseph E. Creed", "Website": "https://www.caterpillar.com", "Ticker": "CAT", "Company type": "Public", "Revenues ($M)": "$67,589", "Profits ($M)": "$8,884", "Market value ($M)": "$429,028", "Number of employees": "118,000", "StockQuote": "NYSE"}, "description": "Caterpillar is a global manufacturer of construction and mining equipment, industrial turbines, engines, and diesel-electric locomotives. Formed from the merger of two competitors in 1925, Caterpillar traces its origins to the fertile San Joaquin Valley, California\u2019s agricultural heartland. The company\u2019s name stems from one of the founders\u2019 inventions, which replaced a steam tractor\u2019s rear wheels with a track system that observers likened to a caterpillar as the machine crawled across soggy terrain. Caterpillar has seen its bright yellow machines become a familiar sight at construction sites around the world, while its employees develop products for industries ranging from oil and gas drilling and power generation to marine and rail technology.", "dataTables": [{"changeHeader": "", "footnote": "", "title": "World's Most Admired Companies", "valueHeader": "", "values": [{"change": null, "title": "Sector", "value": "Transport"}, {"change": null, "title": "Industry", "value": "Construction and Farm Machinery"}, {"change": null, "title": "Current All-Star Rank", "value": "34"}, {"change": null, "title": "Previous All-Star Rank", "value": "40"}, {"change": null, "title": "Industry Rank", "value": "1"}, {"change": null, "title": "Previous Industry Rank", "value": "1"}, {"change": null, "title": "Overall Score", "value": "8.52"}, {"change": null, "title": "Innovation", "value": "2"}, {"change": null, "title": "People Management", "value": "1"}, {"change": null, "title": "Use of Corporate Assets"