16, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 2026, "rank": 65, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "americas-most-innovative-companies", "title": "America's Most Innovative Companies", "year": 2026, "rank": 91, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "worlds-most-admired-companies", "title": "World's Most Admired Companies", "year": 2026, "rank": 34, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "global500", "title": "Fortune Global 500", "year": 2025, "rank": 213, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 2025, "rank": 64, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "americas-most-innovative-companies", "title": "America's Most Innovative Companies", "year": 2025, "rank": 271, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "worlds-most-admired-companies", "title": "World's Most Admired Companies", "year": 2025, "rank": 40, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "global500", "title": "Fortune Global 500", "year": 2024, "rank": 199, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "fortune500--industrials", "title": "Fortune Sector Leaders: Industrials", "year": 2024, "rank": 2, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 2024, "rank": 59, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "worlds-most-admired-companies", "title": "World's Most Admired Companies", "year": 2024, "rank": null, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "worlds-most-admired-companies", "title": "World's Most Admired Companies", "year": 2023, "rank": null, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "global500", "title": "Fortune Global 500", "year": 2023, "rank": 230, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 2023, "rank": 68, "itemDescription": "The 100-year-old construction equipment company rose five spots in 2023 from No. 73 last year. In the 2022 fiscal year, Caterpillar\u2019s sales and revenue rose 16.6% to $59.4 billion, marking one of the best years in company history.<br />\r\n<ul><br />\r\n \t<li>Caterpillar moved its global headquarters from Deerfield, Ill., to Irving, Texas, in 2022.</li><br />\r\n \t<li>To cope with inflation and increasing costs, Caterpillar raised its equipment prices, which helped boost its sales.</li><br />\r\n \t<li>But the heavy-machinery maker still had its fair share of struggles in 2022 in the form of COVID-era supply-chain snarls, inflationary forces, and slow pickup in Chinese demand.</li><br />\r\n \t<li>In October 2022, Caterpillar waived an internal policy that would have required CEO Jim Umpleby to retire when he turns 65, allowing him to continue as the top executive.</li><br />\r\n \t<li>The company is the world\u2019s leading manufacturer of construction and mining equipment, off-highway diesel and natural gas engines, industrial gas turbines, and diesel-electric locomotives, and now has roughly 60% of its operations outside the U.S.</li><br />\r\n</ul>"}, {"slug": "worlds-most-admired-companies", "title": "World's Most Admired Companies", "year": 2022, "rank": null, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "global500", "title": "Fortune Global 500", "year": 2022, "rank": 265, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 2022, "rank": 73, "itemDescription": "<span style=\"font-weight: 400\">Caterpillar recovered some of the ground it lost in 2020 after the pandemic brought construction to a near standstill worldwide. The company climbed five spots on the list this year, with 2021 revenue increasing 22% to $51 billion. Its profits increased dramatically as well, more than doubling. The gains reflected the pent-up demand for Caterpillar\u2019s heavy machinery as construction projects picked up.</span>"}, {"slug": "worlds-most-admired-companies", "title": "World's Most Admired Companies", "year": 2021, "rank": null, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "global500", "title": "Fortune Global 500", "year": 2021, "rank": 283, "itemDescription": "<span data-sheets-value=\"{&quot;1&quot;:2,&quot;2&quot;:&quot;The 96-year-old construction machinery giant continued to slide in the Fortune 500 rankings, dropping 16 spots in 2020. Caterpillar\u2019s bottom line suffered across all regions throughout the pandemic owing to lower demand. But the manufacturing sector has seen recovery start to pick up as more businesses reopen, and total industrial production rose 2.5% year over year in 2020. That, combined with improved commodity prices, hints at a better year ahead for the world\u2019s largest construction-equipment manufacturer.&quot;}\" data-sheets-userformat=\"{&quot;2&quot;:12673,&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:0},&quot;10&quot;:2,&quot;11&quot;:4,&quot;15&quot;:&quot;Calibri, Arial&quot;,&quot;16&quot;:11}\" data-sheets-textstyleruns=\"{&quot;1&quot;:0}\uee10{&quot;1&quot;:71,&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;6&quot;:1}}\uee10{&quot;1&quot;:78}\">The 96-year-old construction machinery giant continued to slide in the Global 500 rankings, dropping 79 spots in 2020. Caterpillar\u2019s bottom line suffered across all regions throughout the pandemic owing to lower demand. But the manufacturing sector has seen recovery start to pick up as more businesses reopen, and total industrial production rose 2.5% year over year in 2020. That, combined with improved commodity prices, hints at a better year ahead for the world\u2019s largest construction-equipment manufacturer.</span>"}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 2021, "rank": 78, "itemDescription": "<span data-sheets-value=\"{&quot;1&quot;:2,&quot;2&quot;:&quot;The 96-year-old construction machinery giant continued to slide in the Fortune 500 rankings, dropping 16 spots in 2020. Caterpillar\u2019s bottom line suffered across all regions throughout the pandemic owing to lower demand. But the manufacturing sector has seen recovery start to pick up as more businesses reopen, and total industrial production rose 2.5% year over year in 2020. That, combined with improved commodity prices, hints at a better year ahead for the world\u2019s largest construction-equipment manufacturer.&quot;}\" data-sheets-userformat=\"{&quot;2&quot;:12673,&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:0},&quot;10&quot;:2,&quot;11&quot;:4,&quot;15&quot;:&quot;Calibri, Arial&quot;,&quot;16&quot;:11}\" data-sheets-textstyleruns=\"{&quot;1&quot;:0}\uee10{&quot;1&quot;:71,&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;6&quot;:1}}\uee10{&quot;1&quot;:78}\">The 96-year-old construction machinery giant continued to slide in the Fortune 500 rankings, dropping 16 spots in 2020. Caterpillar\u2019s bottom line suffered across all regions throughout the pandemic owing to lower demand. But the manufacturing sector has seen recovery start to pick up as more businesses reopen, and total industrial production rose 2.5% year over year in 2020. That, combined with improved commodity prices, hints at a better year ahead for the world\u2019s largest construction-equipment manufacturer.</span>"}, {"slug": "worlds-most-admired-companies", "title": "World's Most Admired Companies", "year": 2020, "rank": 44, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "global500", "title": "Fortune Global 500", "year": 2020, "rank": 204, "itemDescription": "After a stellar 2018, the 95-year-old construction and farm machinery maker slipped a bit in 2019. Total revenue for fiscal 2019 came in at $53.8 billion, down 2% from the year prior. Tensions between the U.S. and China, one of Caterpillar's biggest markets, have hurt sales, and the broader economic slowdown presents an even more daunting near-term challenge. But Caterpillar has given investors incentives to stick with it during a slow patch: The manufacturer returned more than $6 billion in capital to shareholders in 2019, and increased its dividend by 20%."}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 2020, "rank": 62, "itemDescription": "After a stellar 2018, the 95-year-old construction and farm machinery maker slipped a bit in 2019. Total revenue for fiscal 2019 came in at $53.8 billion, down 2% from the year prior. Tensions between the U.S. and China, one of Caterpillar's biggest markets, have hurt sales, and the broader economic slowdown presents an even more daunting near-term challenge. But Caterpillar has given investors incentives to stick with it during a slow patch: The manufacturer returned more than $6 billion in capital to shareholders in 2019, and increased its dividend by 20%."}, {"slug": "worlds-most-admired-companies", "title": "World's Most Admired Companies", "year": 2019, "rank": 43, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "global500", "title": "Fortune Global 500", "year": 2019, "rank": 190, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 2019, "rank": 58, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "worlds-most-admired-companies", "title": "World's Most Admired Companies", "year": 2018, "rank": 43, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "global500", "title": "Fortune Global 500", "year": 2018, "rank": 238, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 2018, "rank": 65, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "worlds-most-admired-companies", "title": "World's Most Admired Companies", "year": 2017, "rank": 47, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "global500", "title": "Fortune Global 500", "year": 2017, "rank": 264, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 2017, "rank": 74, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "worlds-most-admired-companies", "title": "World's Most Admired Companies", "year": 2016, "rank": 45, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "global500", "title": "Fortune Global 500", "year": 2016, "rank": 194, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 2016, "rank": 59, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "worlds-most-admired-companies", "title": "World's Most Admired Companies", "year": 2015, "rank": 28, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "global500", "title": "Fortune Global 500", "year": 2015, "rank": 187, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 2015, "rank": 54, "itemDescription": ""